127I  c  Phys Rev C xxx, xxxxxx (2025).                                         
127I  c  2025LaAA: E=50 MeV {+7}Li beam was produced from the 15UD Pelletron    
127I 2c  accelerator at the Inter University Accelerator Center (IUAC), New     
127I 3c  Delhi, India. Target was a isotopically enriched (99.4%) and           
127I 4c  self-supported {+124}Sn metal foil of thickness of 2.7 mg/cm{+2}. The  
127I 5c  high-spin states of {+127}I were populated via the                     
127I 6c  {+124}Sn({+7}Li,4n){+127}I fusion-evaporation reaction and the         
127I 7c  deexciting |g rays were detected using the Indian National Gamma Array 
127I 8c  (INGA) consisting of 15 HPGe Compton-suppressed clover detectors at    
127I 9c  32|' (three), 57|' (two), 90|' (four), 123|' (two), and 148|' (four).  
127I Ac  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin. Deduced levels, J, |p, T{-1/2} using the 
127I Bc  Doppler-Shift Attenuation Method (DSAM) lineshape analysis, and        
127I Cc  transition strengths. Comparisons with the single quasi-particle rotor 
127I Dc  model calculations.                                                    
127I  cG E,M$From 2025LaAA.                                                     
127I  cG E(X)$Newly observed |g transitions in 2025LaAA.                        
127I  cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies (by compiler).           
